    {
      "id": "12e5ce30563d",
      "name": "nightly-hermes-github-backup",
      "prompt": "Perform the nightly Hermes backup to GitHub. This is a disaster-recovery sync — push skills, memory, config templates, and other durable Hermes state to the private GitHub repo so a fresh Hermes can be rebuilt from scratch if the VPS is corrupted.\n\nTARGET REPO: https://github.com/theduy3/hermes-zeus-backup\nAUTH: GITHUB_TOKEN from ~/.hermes/.env (scoped to repo, read+write contents)\n\n── SELF-CHECK: IS IT MIDNIGHT VANCOUVER? ──\n\nThis cron is scheduled for 00:00 America/Toronto local time. Do this check first:\n\n1. Determine the current hour in America/Toronto timezone. Use `python3` if available, otherwise `TZ=America/Toronto date +%H`.\n2. If the hour is 00 (midnight) → proceed to the sync steps below.\n3. For any other hour, do not run the backup; report the current America/Toronto time and say the schedule may need adjustment.\n\n── SYNC STEPS ──\n\nOnce midnight Vancouver is confirmed:\n\n1. cd ~/.hermes/\n\n2. Verify the repo is initialized:\n   - Check for .git directory. If missing, run: git init && git remote add origin https://$(grep GITHUB_TOKEN .env | cut -d= -f2)@github.com/theduy3/hermes-zeus-backup.git\n   - Verify remote exists.\n\n3. Ensure .gitignore exists (create it if missing) — must exclude at minimum: .env, auth.json, logs/, sessions/, audio_cache/, hermes-agent/, .git-credentials\n\n4. Set git identity if not configured:\n   git config user.name \"Hermes Agent\" && git config user.email \"hermes@vps\"\n\n5. Stage all changes:\n   git add -A\n\n6. Check if there are any changes to commit (git diff --cached --quiet). If no changes, report \"No changes to sync\" and exit. If there are changes:\n\n7. Generate a meaningful commit message — include a timestamp (America/Toronto) and a summary of what changed (e.g., \"nightly sync: updated 3 skills, 1 memory entry\"). Use `git diff --cached --stat` to see what files changed.\n\n8. Commit and push:\n   git commit -m \"nightly sync: ...\"\n   git push origin main\n\n9. Report: commit hash, files changed, push status.\n\n── FAILURE HANDLING ──\n\nIf any step fails (no network, token expired, etc.):\n- Report the specific failure clearly\n- Do NOT retry more than once on network errors\n- If the token appears expired or invalid, say so explicitly\n\n── IMPORTANT ──\n\nNEVER commit .env, auth.json, or any file containing API keys/tokens/secrets. If git add -A somehow stages a secret file, unstage it before committing. The .gitignore should prevent this, but double-check: `git diff --cached --name-only | grep -E '\\.env$|auth\\.json|\\.pem$|\\.key$'` — if anything matches, unstage those files with `git reset HEAD -- <file>` before committing.",
